menu "Water Tank Sensor"

    config WT_SENSOR_UART_NUM
        int "UART port used for the A02YYUW sensor"
        range 1 2
        default 2
        help
            Hardware UART connected to the sensor. UART0 is the console/flashing port
            and must not be used here.

    config WT_SENSOR_RX_GPIO
        int "ESP32 RX GPIO (wired to sensor TX, white wire)"
        range 0 39
        default 16
        help
            GPIO receiving the sensor's 9600 baud data frames. Swap with the TX GPIO
            if no data is received and the wiring is reversed (gap G1).
            Note: on ESP32-WROVER modules GPIO16/17 are used by the PSRAM (gap G2).
            GPIO6-11 (SPI flash) and the non-existent GPIO20, 24 and 28-31 are
            rejected at boot: a02yyuw_init logs an error and the firmware aborts.

    config WT_SENSOR_TX_GPIO
        int "ESP32 TX GPIO (wired to sensor RX, yellow wire); -1 = unused"
        range -1 33
        default 17
        help
            The firmware never transmits to the sensor. The idle-HIGH UART TX line
            keeps the sensor in its "processed value" output mode, which is the
            same as leaving the sensor RX wire unconnected. Set to -1 to leave the
            pin unconfigured. Must differ from the RX GPIO. GPIO6-11 (SPI flash) and
            the non-existent GPIO20, 24 and 28-31 are rejected at boot.
            Use -1 while the pin direction is unconfirmed: if the sensor TX wire
            is on this pin, the driven-HIGH TX line would fight the sensor output.

    config WT_REPORT_PERIOD_MS
        int "Distance report period (ms)"
        range 100 60000
        default 1000
        help
            Interval between distance lines printed on the console.

    config WT_SENSOR_STALE_MS
        int "Sensor data stale timeout (ms)"
        range 200 10000
        default 1000
        help
            If no checksum-valid frame was received for longer than this, the
            report shows status=NO_DATA.

    config WT_MEDIAN_FILTER
        bool "Enable median filter on sensor readings"
        default n
        help
            Report the median of the last N valid frames instead of the newest
            raw frame. Useful against splash/condensation outliers.

    config WT_MEDIAN_WINDOW
        int "Median filter window (frames)"
        depends on WT_MEDIAN_FILTER
        range 3 15
        default 5

endmenu
